{
  "$schema": "./SCHEMA.md#ledger-entry-hash",
  "description": "The ledger entry hash (avalon_protocol::ledger_entry, domain tag avalon.ledger.entry). entryHashHex is the SHA-256 of signingBytesHex, which is the tag (ASCII, no length), the entry version as u16 big-endian, then networkId and shardId (u32 BE length and UTF-8), seq as u64 BE, prevHashHex (32 raw bytes), eventId (16 raw bytes), kind, issuer and subject (u32 BE length and UTF-8), the payload hash (32 raw bytes) and timestampUnixMicros as i64 BE. The payload hash is the SHA-256 of the canonical payload (canonical-payload.json) so a row with a pruned payload still verifies: skeleton vectors give payloadHashHex instead of payloadJsonUtf8. A timestamp is the instant truncated (toward negative infinity) to unix microseconds. prevHashHex, payloadHashHex are exactly 64 lowercase hex characters, seq is a decimal string in 0..2^64-1 and version is 0..65535; anything else must be rejected with expected.error (invalid_hash or out_of_range). Generated by scripts/gen-ledger-entry-vectors.py, an encoder independent of the Rust one.",
  "supportedIn": [
    "rust",
    "csharp",
    "typescript"
  ],
